# Claude Code's project directory is machine-local: settings in here can hold
# your course API key, and this repo goes public when you ship. Your tracked
# harness is CLAUDE.md (and any AGENTS.md), not this directory.
.claude/

# The SOURCE assets: 84 MB of glTF models, 4K textures and audio. `pnpm assets`
# builds the shipping copies in public/assets/ from these, so only the derived,
# committed output is in history. Keeping the sources out means a re-encode is a
# rebuild rather than a second permanent copy in every clone.
#
# The whole tree is ignored, and it is deliberately NOT called `assets/`. A
# directory of that name in the repo root is served at the same URL as
# public/assets/, so `/assets/f15/scene.gltf` had two files behind it and vite
# picked between them by timing -- dev served the source and looked perfect
# while the build, which copies only public/, shipped a site where every model
# 404'd. See scripts/compress-assets.ts.
assets-src/
